x86_64-windows  a class-typed throw needs the Microsoft ThrowInfo chain pointed at a class: a type descriptor per class, a catchable type per class, and a _CTA array listing the thrown class AND its bases - which is how catch-by-base works on that ABI, where Itanium walks __si_class_type_info instead. Measured from clang for this target: throwing a Derived emits ??_R0?AUDerived@@@8 and ??_R0?AUBase@@@8, _CT??_R0?AU...@84 for each, _CTA2?AUDerived@@ and _TI2?AUDerived@@. cxx1 emits the four objects for a fundamental type only, and refuses a class by name. Its own step.
